#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:-1
msgid "digiKam Export to Immich Web-Service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:-1
msgid ""
"digiKam, documentation, user manual, photo management, open source, free, "
"learn, easy, immich, export, self-hosted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:14
msgid ":ref:`Export To Immich <export_tools>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:16
msgid "This tool allows the user to upload photos to an Immich server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:18
msgid ""
"`Immich <https://immich.app/>`_ is an open source, self-hosted photo and "
"video backup platform. You run the Immich server yourself, on your own "
"hardware, and this tool connects digiKam to that server so the photos you "
"manage and edit in digiKam can be published to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:20
msgid ""
"The plugin also provides a companion download tool, described in the :ref:"
"`Import from Immich <immich_import>` chapter. Both tools share a single "
"window and the same connection settings, and each opens in its own mode: "
"this one from the :menuselection:`Export --> Export to Immich` menu entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:22
msgid ""
"Before the tool can do anything, it must connect to your server. At the top "
"of the window, enter the **Server URL** of your Immich server and the **API "
"key** to authenticate with, then press the **Connect** button. The tool "
"checks the settings, stores them for the next sessions, and loads the list "
"of albums from the server. The API key is kept in the KDE wallet when one is "
"available. With stored settings, the tool connects automatically when it "
"opens, and pressing **Connect** again reloads the albums, for example after "
"albums have been created or renamed in the Immich web interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:24
msgid ""
"You create an API key in the Immich web interface, under :menuselection:"
"`Account Settings --> API Keys`. The key needs the ``asset.upload``, ``asset."
"read``, ``asset.view``, ``asset.download``, ``album.read``, ``album."
"create``, ``albumAsset.create`` and ``tag.read`` permissions. Updating the "
"metadata of photos already on the server additionally needs ``asset."
"update``, ``tag.create`` and ``tag.asset``. Stacking a replacement photo on "
"top of its previous version needs ``stack.create`` and ``stack.read``, and "
"sending the previous version to the trash needs ``asset.delete``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:30
msgid "The Immich Export Tool Dialog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:32
msgid ""
"By default, the tool uploads the items currently selected in digiKam. The "
"selected items are shown as thumbnails in the window, and the selection made "
"in digiKam is the upload set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:34
msgid ""
"With the **Upload to** options, you choose where the photos go on the "
"server. **Library only**, the default, uploads them into the library without "
"assigning an album. The alternative is an album, chosen from the album tiles "
"below: the tiles are sorted by name, a filter field narrows the list, and "
"the **New Album** button creates a new album on the server. The chosen "
"target is remembered for the next session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:36
msgid ""
"The **Edited photos** option decides what happens when a photo you upload is "
"recognised as a new version of one the server already has, as described in "
"the re-exporting section below. **Stack**, the default, places the new "
"version on top of the old one as the primary of a stack. **Overwrite** sends "
"the old version to the Immich trash instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:42
msgid "The Immich Export Uploading in Progress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:44
msgid ""
"Press the **Upload selection** button to transfer the items. A progress bar "
"follows the transfer, the **Cancel** button aborts it, and when the transfer "
"ends a line in the window summarises the outcome, with the counts of "
"uploaded, updated and skipped items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:47
msgid "Re-exporting Photos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:49
msgid ""
"Exporting the same selection again is safe, and never produces a duplicate "
"on the server. The tool recognises a file as one the server already has from "
"its file name, capture time and dimensions, confirmed by comparing its "
"pixels with the server copy. What happens next depends on what changed since "
"the last export:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:51
msgid ""
"If nothing changed, nothing is uploaded, and only metadata differences are "
"written, as below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:53
msgid ""
"If only the metadata changed, the pixels being identical, nothing is "
"uploaded either. The changed tags, rating, caption and GPS position are "
"written to the existing photo on the server through the API. Tag changes are "
"additive: a tag removed in digiKam is not removed on the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:55
msgid ""
"If the picture itself was edited, the new version is uploaded and added to "
"every album the old version belonged to. With **Stack**, it becomes the "
"primary of a stack with the old version. With **Overwrite**, the old version "
"is moved to the Immich trash, where it can be recovered for 30 days. In both "
"cases the replacement is a new photo on the server: links shared from the "
"old version do not carry over, and edits made to the old version inside "
"Immich are lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:57
msgid ""
"If the photo was cropped or resized, so its dimensions no longer match, it "
"is only replaced when a check confirms the local image is a crop of the "
"server photo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:59
msgid ""
"If the evidence is ambiguous, nothing is overwritten or stacked, and the "
"file is uploaded as a new photo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:61
msgid ""
"A renamed file cannot be recognised, because recognition needs the file name "
"and the capture time to survive the edit. Files the tool cannot decode, such "
"as RAW files, are never replaced or stacked; their metadata still "
"synchronises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:64
msgid "How Metadata Travels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:66
msgid ""
"Metadata travels between digiKam and Immich in XMP sidecar files, which both "
"applications read and write. On upload, the tool generates a sidecar from "
"the metadata in digiKam's database, holding the tags, the rating, the "
"caption and the GPS position, and merges it over the file's existing XMP, so "
"properties the tool does not set, colour labels included, survive the round "
"trip. On download, the sidecar written by Immich is stored next to each "
"original."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export_tools/immich_export.rst:68
msgid ""
"Pixel edits do not travel in XMP. Only rendered exports, such as JPEG or "
"TIFF files, carry pixel changes back to Immich."
msgstr ""
